  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \nHot conditions will be present today with highs in the upper 80s to\nlower 90s. Some heat index values will be around 100. Cooler\ntemperatures are expected the next couple of days with cloud cover,\ncooler air, and precipitation. Temperatures will gradually start to\nrise over the weekend and into next week.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2) \nThunderstorms will work into the region this afternoon into the\nevening hours. Some of these storms will have the potential to be\nsevere with damaging winds the primary threat. Thunderstorms will\nlinger into the night, however expect some decrease in activity for a\nperiod overnight. Another surge of moisture will work into the region\non Thursday bringing additional showers and thunderstorms. The\nheaviest precipitation amounts on Thursday are expected to be across\nthe southern half of the forecast area. Will have to watch for the\npotential for multiple thunderstorms moving across the area\nespecially across southern portions of the region and the potential\nfor flash flooding. Confidence was not high enough however to go with\na flood watch. \n\nAdditional showers and storms will be possible on Friday, primarily\nacross southern portions of the region. Coverage works northward\nFriday night into Saturday.",
